In getSequence, add to the shared error list only under the exclusive lock (libs/axf/restore-read.c).

When a reference fails to open, getSequence records the error in the error list shared by every
RestoreRead in the process, but holds only the shared lock while it does. Threads that fail at
the same time realloc and shift the list together, and other threads binary-search it meanwhile,
so the list (and the heap) can be corrupted: double frees and crashes in realloc or when the
shared state is freed. The insert now takes the exclusive lock, and searches the list again
first, since other threads may have changed it since the earlier search. Upstream:
https://github.com/ncbi/ncbi-vdb/pull/290. Drop this patch once the vendored ncbi-vdb includes it.

--- a/libs/axf/restore-read.c
+++ b/libs/axf/restore-read.c
@@ -556,7 +556,12 @@
         // it is a new seq_id
         rc = openSeqID(self, id_len, wgs_namelen, seq_id, forTable);
         if (rc) {
-            Error_Insert(&self->shared->errors, error_at, id_len, seq_id, rc);
+            /* The error list is shared: change it only under the exclusive lock, and search it
+             * again, since other threads may have changed it since the search above. */
+            RestoreReadSharedWriter(self->shared);
+            if (!Error_Find(&self->shared->errors, &error_at, id_len, seq_id))
+                Error_Insert(&self->shared->errors, error_at, id_len, seq_id, rc);
+            RestoreReadSharedWriterDone(self->shared);
             return rc;
         }
     }
